    <description><![CDATA[A beautiful client for Plex & Jellyfin

Stream your media library with HDR, Dolby Vision, offline downloads, and a gorgeous experience across all your devices.

**Features**

- Wide Codec Support
- HDR10+
- Subtitles
- Cross-Platform
- Offline
- Watch Together
- Tracker Sync
- Skip intros
- Chapter support
- Gestures
]]></description>
    <summary>A modern client for Plex and Jellyfin on desktop, mobile, and TV. Built with Flutter for native performance and a clean interface.</summary>
    <releaseNotes><![CDATA[[Releases](https://github.com/edde746/plezy/releases)

## New features

- Audio and subtitle sync sliders cover ±10 seconds in 50 ms steps
- The bundled ffmpeg enables the loudnorm filter for volume normalization

## Playback

- Plex video transcodes use fMP4 HLS, so HEVC presets stop corrupting
- Plex transcodes seek in-band instead of pre-warming at the resume offset
- Same-day Specials no longer hijack up next
- Episode advances that fail on a transient server blip are retried
- Playback no longer fails when a preference write is refused
- TrueHD offers its MAT carrier on Android 10–12 audio routes
- Timeline heartbeats stop once a Plex server terminates the session
- ExoPlayer track labels say AAC instead of mp4a.40.2
- Emby scrub previews load from the server's BIF index
- iOS and tvOS keep HDR and Dolby Vision when the video is zoomed
- tvOS schedules frames with more presentation lead

## Subtitles

- Korean glyphs render on the MPV path via a bundled Hangul font
- Disabling subtitles clears the displayed ASS cue immediately
- ASS frames that overflow the glyph atlas render as a flattened composite
- External subtitle files load with the media whether or not they are selected
- Android renders every PGS composition object and keeps the PGS display-plane aspect

## Music

- Hardware media keys work while the app is in the foreground on Android
- iOS music playback gains lock-screen and headphone controls

## Plex

- Live TV favorite updates persist again
- PIN sign-in keeps polling after transient network errors

## Watch Together

- Lobby guests are told the room's control mode

## Downloads & profiles

- The parallel download limit stays intact on slow networks
- Offline downloads stay visible when a profile's servers are unreachable

## Android, TV & automotive

- MKV files with late track metadata play again
- A backgrounded TV stops the server session when it releases the player
- Quality labels stay visible when rating badges crowd the detail line
- TV pauses on the first Select press after skipping the intro
- Parked playback is no longer blocked when the car service gives no verdict
- The background Watch Next refresh is removed

## UI

- The sidebar's Libraries section stays collapsed across restarts
- Phone back exits the player even with the controls up
- Escape leaves fullscreen instead of quitting the app on desktop
- Player, downloads and server-setup text that was left in English is now translated

## macOS

- Every audio format, including compressed formats, routes through CoreAudio

## Windows

- The MSVC runtime is bundled, so an outdated redistributable no longer crashes launch

## Linux

- VAAPI hardware decode and AV1 software fallback are restored in the bundled libmpv
- The Flutter-texture fallback is removed; video always renders on the native Wayland plane
- HDR transactions and plane presentation are bounded against unacknowledged frames]]></releaseNotes>
